{"explanation":"Extends the existing instrumented coverage using only the supplied public EncryptedKey API. The added repeated-encryption test verifies that two encryptions of the same plaintext key under one AES key create distinct EncryptedKey instances and that both records decrypt with their original bytes and algorithm. The existing round-trip test is renamed to describe the algorithm/AAD-selector preservation it observes, and UTF-8 plaintext encoding is made explicit. The supplied API surface exposes no serialization or GCM-parameter/nonce accessor, so this test cannot soundly construct, inspect, or tamper with serialized legacy records without an evidenced production test seam or reflection.","review_assumptions":["EncryptedKey.decrypt reconstructs the persisted plaintext-key algorithm/AAD selector as stated by the preceding EncryptedKey contract; the algorithm assertion observes that preservation through the public API.","The public EncryptedKey API supplied for this batch has only encrypt(SecretKey, SecretKey) and decrypt(SecretKey). It provides no documented serialization, deserialization, cipher-algorithm, AlgorithmParameters, ciphertext, AAD-selector, or nonce inspection operation. Consequently, legacy-fixture and concrete nonce-parameter assertions require a production-owned, package-private test seam or another evidenced public API; this draft does not invent either or use reflection.","Distinct EncryptedKey object identity confirms separate record creation but cannot by itself prove distinct GCM nonce values. Android-provider review must validate the explicit GCMParameterSpec initialization and persisted AlgorithmParameters behavior required by the production EncryptedKey change."],"no_change_required":false,"decision":"MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW","confidence":"medium","edits":[{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/EncryptedKeyTest.java","original_code":"@RunWith(AndroidJUnit4.class)
public class EncryptedKeyTest extends TestCase {
    private SecretKey generateKey(String algorithm) throws NoSuchAlgorithmException {
        KeyGenerator kg = KeyGenerator.getInstance(algorithm);
        kg.init(256);
        return kg.generateKey();
    }

    @Test
    public void test() throws GeneralSecurityException, IOException {
        SecretKey tok = generateKey("HmacSHA512");
        SecretKey key = generateKey("AES");

        EncryptedKey ek = EncryptedKey.encrypt(key, tok);
        SecretKey res = ek.decrypt(key);

        Assert.assertArrayEquals(tok.getEncoded(), res.getEncoded());
        assertEquals(tok.getAlgorithm(), res.getAlgorithm());
    }

    @Test
    public void testUTF8() throws GeneralSecurityException, IOException {
        String plaintxt = "火尸木火1十寥日烤";
        SecretKey key = generateKey("AES");

        byte[] plaintxt_encoded = plaintxt.getBytes();

        SecretKey plaintxt_key = new SecretKeySpec(plaintxt_encoded, "AES");
        EncryptedKey ek = EncryptedKey.encrypt(key, plaintxt_key);

        SecretKey sk = ek.decrypt(key);
        byte[] decryptedBytes = sk.getEncoded();
        String decryptedText = new String(decryptedBytes, StandardCharsets.UTF_8);

        assertEquals(plaintxt, decryptedText);
    }
}
","edit_kind":"test","corrected_code":"@RunWith(AndroidJUnit4.class)
public class EncryptedKeyTest extends TestCase {
    private SecretKey generateKey(String algorithm) throws NoSuchAlgorithmException {
        KeyGenerator kg = KeyGenerator.getInstance(algorithm);
        kg.init(256);
        return kg.generateKey();
    }

    @Test
    public void encryptDecryptPreservesEncodedKeyAndAlgorithm() throws GeneralSecurityException, IOException {
        SecretKey tok = generateKey("HmacSHA512");
        SecretKey key = generateKey("AES");

        EncryptedKey ek = EncryptedKey.encrypt(key, tok);
        SecretKey res = ek.decrypt(key);

        Assert.assertArrayEquals(tok.getEncoded(), res.getEncoded());
        assertEquals(tok.getAlgorithm(), res.getAlgorithm());
    }

    @Test
    public void repeatedEncryptionsCreateDistinctDecryptableRecords() throws GeneralSecurityException, IOException {
        SecretKey tok = generateKey("HmacSHA512");
        SecretKey key = generateKey("AES");

        EncryptedKey first = EncryptedKey.encrypt(key, tok);
        EncryptedKey second = EncryptedKey.encrypt(key, tok);

        Assert.assertNotSame(first, second);

        SecretKey firstResult = first.decrypt(key);
        SecretKey secondResult = second.decrypt(key);
        Assert.assertArrayEquals(tok.getEncoded(), firstResult.getEncoded());
        Assert.assertArrayEquals(tok.getEncoded(), secondResult.getEncoded());
        assertEquals(tok.getAlgorithm(), firstResult.getAlgorithm());
        assertEquals(tok.getAlgorithm(), secondResult.getAlgorithm());
    }

    @Test
    public void testUTF8() throws GeneralSecurityException, IOException {
        String plaintxt = "火尸木火1十寥日烤";
        SecretKey key = generateKey("AES");

        byte[] plaintxt_encoded = plaintxt.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8);

        SecretKey plaintxt_key = new SecretKeySpec(plaintxt_encoded, "AES");
        EncryptedKey ek = EncryptedKey.encrypt(key, plaintxt_key);

        SecretKey sk = ek.decrypt(key);
        byte[] decryptedBytes = sk.getEncoded();
        String decryptedText = new String(decryptedBytes, StandardCharsets.UTF_8);

        assertEquals(plaintxt, decryptedText);
    }
}
","reason":"Adds public-API instrumented coverage for repeated encryption and decryptability while preserving the existing encoded-key/algorithm and UTF-8 round trips. This test deliberately avoids unsupported serialization and nonce introspection because neither is present in the evidenced EncryptedKey API surface." ,"symbol":"EncryptedKey encrypt/decrypt test cases"}],"manual_review_required":true,"provided_contracts":["The instrumented tests continue to call only EncryptedKey.encrypt(SecretKey, SecretKey) and EncryptedKey.decrypt(SecretKey).","The tests exercise encoded-key and algorithm preservation for a generated HmacSHA512 key and separate successful decryptions of two records created under one AES key."],"required_contracts":["EncryptedKey.encrypt must retain public signature encrypt(SecretKey, SecretKey), AES/GCM/NoPadding, explicit fresh 96-bit GCM nonce preparation, and a 128-bit authentication tag specification.","EncryptedKey must continue to persist and reconstruct AlgorithmParameters, ciphertext, cipher transformation, and plaintext-key algorithm/AAD-selector data for decryption.","A production-owned test seam or documented API is required before this test class can verify concrete serialized legacy fixtures and GCM parameter/nonce values without reflection.","MasterKey and Encryptor must retain EncryptedKey.encrypt(SecretKey, SecretKey) as their caller entry point and preserve deployed-record decryption."],"source_file_path":"mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/EncryptedKeyTest.java","required_tests":["Run the Android instrumentation tests in EncryptedKeyTest.","After an evidenced serialization/parameter inspection seam exists, add a fixed pre-change serialized-record fixture test and assert successful decryption.","After that seam exists, assert repeated encryptions use distinct concrete GCM nonce/AlgorithmParameters values and that records remain decryptable after serialization."]}
